CRASH-19: stop EN_addrule writing into the caller's rule text

EN_addrule split the rule text into lines by writing '\0' over each
newline of the caller's string, and put the newline back only after the
line had been parsed. A string literal therefore faulted, and a rule
with an error was left cut short in the caller's buffer. EN_addrule now
finds the end of each line and copies that many characters into its
own buffer, line2, so the caller's string is only read. The prototype
keeps its char * argument.

Requires: CRASH-18

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb, after CRASH-18:
    git apply CRASH-19_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 2c5a115..8f99a10 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -5646,18 +5646,18 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_addrule(EN_Project p, char *rule)
     {
         // Find where current line ends and next one begins
         nextline = strchr(line, '\n');
-        if (nextline) *nextline = '\0';
+        if (nextline == NULL) nextline = line + strlen(line);
 
         // The line and the newline added below must fit in line2
-        if (strlen(line) >= MAXLINE)
+        if (nextline - line >= MAXLINE)
         {
             rules->Errcode = 214;
             break;
         }
 
-        // Copy and tokenize the current line
-        strcpy(line2, line);
-        strcat(line2, "\n");  // Tokenizer won't work without this
+        // Copy the current line and a newline (the tokenizer needs it)
+        // into line2 and tokenize it; the caller's string is only read
+        sprintf(line2, "%.*s\n", (int)(nextline - line), line);
         parser->Ntokens = gettokens(line2, parser->Tok, MAXTOKS, parser->Comment);
 
         // Process the line to build up the rule's contents
@@ -5668,8 +5668,7 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_addrule(EN_Project p, char *rule)
         }
 
         // Extract next line from the rule statement
-        if (nextline) *nextline = '\n';
-        line = nextline ? (nextline + 1) : NULL;
+        line = *nextline ? (nextline + 1) : NULL;
     }
 
     // Delete new rule entry if there was an error
